# PREPARED, NOT ACTIVE — see README.md in this directory and ADR-009.
#
# Only relevant if/when Cloudflare Tunnel is ever removed from the ingress
# path (direct DNS -> VM public IP instead). Today (2026-08-29) that is
# NOT the plan: multi-cloud-strategy.md keeps Cloudflare as the routing
# layer through every phase (local -> oci-free -> aws-prod -> multi-cloud),
# tunnel just relocates. This file exists so the answer to "what if we
# ever need our own reverse proxy" is a tested config, not a blank page.
#
# Targets mirror tunnel/cloudflared/config.yml's ingress list exactly --
# same hostnames, same ports (see docs/reference/network-topology.md's
# port map) -- so activating this later means swapping the ingress
# mechanism, not redesigning routing.
#
# Caddy gets automatic HTTPS (Let's Encrypt) for free -- no cert config
# below is intentional, not an oversight.

